## Common requires Patterns

### Pattern 1: Non-Null Checks
```xiom
fn process(data: *Int)
  requires: data != null;
{ /* safe to dereference */ }
```

### Pattern 2: Range Validation
```xiom
fn clamp(value: Int, min: Int, max: Int) -> Int
  requires: min <= max;
{ if value < min { return min; } if value > max { return max; } return value; }
```

### Pattern 3: Non-Empty Collections
```xiom
fn first[T](items: &Vec[T]) -> T
  requires: items.len() > 0;
{ return items[0]; }
```

### Pattern 4: Valid Index
```xiom
fn get[T](arr: &Vec[T], index: Int) -> T
  requires: index >= 0;
  requires: index < arr.len();
{ return arr[index]; }
```

### Pattern 5: Argument Relationships
```xiom
fn substring(s: Str, start: Int, end: Int) -> Str
  requires: start >= 0;
  requires: end <= s.len();
  requires: start <= end;
{ /* safe to slice */ }
```

### Pattern 6: Resource State
```xiom
fn read(file: &File) -> Str
  requires: file.is_open();
  requires: file.is_readable();
{ /* safe to read */ }
```

### Pattern 7: Mathematical Constraints
```xiom
fn sqrt(n: Float64) -> Float64
  requires: n >= 0.0;
{ /* safe to compute */ }
```

